      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Natchez was the southern terminus of the historic Natchez Trace, a trail that stretched north to Nashville, Tennessee.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natchez%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The city sits on the Mississippi River opposite Vidalia, Louisiana, and was a major cotton planter hub in the antebellum era.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natchez%2C_Mississippi",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Natchez is home to the oldest European settlement in the lower Mississippi Valley, founded by French colonists in 1716.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
